The City fire department issues this schedule. The complete Construction Plan Check Fee definition identifies Pikes Peak Regional Building Department (PPRBD) as the collector through its plan portal; this does not reassign the issuing authority. Accela submission is separately described for the fire-system plan-check fee.

**Mandatory shared context for every result**

**GENERAL-PLAN-REVIEW**

Unless otherwise noted, a plan review fee includes two plan reviews, an initial inspection, and a final <br>inspection. Additional fees may be assessed for subsequent reviews, trips, and re-inspections. 

[Physical page 2](</Users/mcoors/Documents/Project Geode/MasterLegalDatabase/research/local_review/colorado-springs-construction-fees-qa-2026-09-12/images/page-2.png>)


**IMPLEMENTATION**

Implementation: Fees shall be assessed upon the plan approval date. 

[Physical page 7](</Users/mcoors/Documents/Project Geode/MasterLegalDatabase/research/local_review/colorado-springs-construction-fees-qa-2026-09-12/images/page-7.png>)


**OTHER-SCHEDULE**

Note Worthy  <br>Fees associated with high pile storage and hazardous materials are listed in the Colorado Springs Fire <br>Department Code Services Fee Schedule. 

[Physical page 7](</Users/mcoors/Documents/Project Geode/MasterLegalDatabase/research/local_review/colorado-springs-construction-fees-qa-2026-09-12/images/page-7.png>)


**P4-MISC-01 — physical page 4**

- Label: Technology Fee – assessed on all permits 
- Source fee text: $25.00 

[Page image](</Users/mcoors/Documents/Project Geode/MasterLegalDatabase/research/local_review/colorado-springs-construction-fees-qa-2026-09-12/images/page-4.png>)

**Complete source definitions and table notes**

**SPRINKLER-INSPECTIONS**

NOTE: Three sprinkler system inspections shall be allowed, per permit, prior to assessing a trip fee for <br>additional inspections. 

[Physical page 4](</Users/mcoors/Documents/Project Geode/MasterLegalDatabase/research/local_review/colorado-springs-construction-fees-qa-2026-09-12/images/page-4.png>)


**REINSPECTION-NOTE**

NOTE:  A re-inspection fee may be applied if the site is inaccessible and/or work is not sufficiently pre-<br>tested, or hazards are not completed in the required timeframe. 

[Physical page 5](</Users/mcoors/Documents/Project Geode/MasterLegalDatabase/research/local_review/colorado-springs-construction-fees-qa-2026-09-12/images/page-5.png>)


**EXTRATERRITORIAL-NOTE**

NOTE: Extraterritorial fees shall be applied when a plan review and an inspection is requested for projects <br>outside the City of Colorado Springs’ jurisdiction. In addition to all applicable fees, a one-time surcharge <br>shall be assessed based on the inspector’s travel-time and roundtrip mileage. Mileage shall be calculated <br>using each city’s center point, as referenced on Google Maps. Mileage shall be calculated at the current <br>Internal Revenue Service’s (IRS) standard mileage rate. Surcharges will be rounded to the nearest dollar. 

[Physical page 5](</Users/mcoors/Documents/Project Geode/MasterLegalDatabase/research/local_review/colorado-springs-construction-fees-qa-2026-09-12/images/page-5.png>)


**DEF-ADMINISTRATIVE**

Administrative Support: This hourly fee will be charged for the time it takes CSFD administrative staff to <br>conduct record searches for expired permits, plans or inspection reports for current active projects, and <br>inspection requests when record number is not provided at time of request.     

[Physical page 6](</Users/mcoors/Documents/Project Geode/MasterLegalDatabase/research/local_review/colorado-springs-construction-fees-qa-2026-09-12/images/page-6.png>)


**DEF-CONSTRUCTION-PLAN-CHECK**

Construction Plan Check Fee: This fee will be collected by Pikes Peak Regional Building Department (PPRBD) <br>upon plans being submitted through PPRBD’s plan portal.  This fee equates to a limited review, which is <br>the smallest amount that CSFD will charge for review of a construction plan set.  If a full review and <br>inspection is required for the project, then the plan check fee will be deducted from the total fee charged <br>at time of CSFD plan approval.   

[Physical page 6](</Users/mcoors/Documents/Project Geode/MasterLegalDatabase/research/local_review/colorado-springs-construction-fees-qa-2026-09-12/images/page-6.png>)


**DEF-CONVENIENCE**

Convenience Inspection: A convenience inspection fee is assessed when a business or contractor requests <br>an inspection outside the normal business hours of the Division of the Fire Marshal to accommodate their <br>convenience.   

[Physical page 6](</Users/mcoors/Documents/Project Geode/MasterLegalDatabase/research/local_review/colorado-springs-construction-fees-qa-2026-09-12/images/page-6.png>)


**DEF-EXPEDITED**

Expedited Plan Review: Allows plans to be moved to the front of the plan review queue.  Expedited plan <br>reviews are available for all plans reviewed by the Division of the Fire Marshal, including extraterritorial <br>reviews.  Expedited plan reviews are available on a first-come first-served basis, and the fee shall be paid <br>at the time of the request.  The availability of expedited plan reviews are at the discretion of the fire code <br>official based on staffing and/or resource availability.  Expedited plan reviews do not supersede rapid <br>response reviews. 

[Physical page 6](</Users/mcoors/Documents/Project Geode/MasterLegalDatabase/research/local_review/colorado-springs-construction-fees-qa-2026-09-12/images/page-6.png>)


**DEF-FIRE-PLAN-CHECK**

Fire sprinkler, fire alarm, fixed fire, and water plan check fee:  This fee will be assessed at time of these <br>plans being submitted in Accela.  This fee must be paid before plans are checked in for review.  This fee <br>applies to all fire sprinkler, fire alarm, and fire suppression plans including 5-device letters and 20-head <br>letters.   

[Physical page 6](</Users/mcoors/Documents/Project Geode/MasterLegalDatabase/research/local_review/colorado-springs-construction-fees-qa-2026-09-12/images/page-6.png>)


**DEF-HIGH-RISE**

High-Rise Building Surcharge: A one-time fee to cover the additional time for review, inspection and <br>building commissioning that accompanies the complex nature of all high-rise structures. 

[Physical page 6](</Users/mcoors/Documents/Project Geode/MasterLegalDatabase/research/local_review/colorado-springs-construction-fees-qa-2026-09-12/images/page-6.png>)


**DEF-LIMITED-REVIEW**

Limited Review: A limited review is when a review is performed by Fire Construction Services of a <br>construction plan and the scope of work does not impact life safety and therefore the plans is marked “not <br>applicable”, and no fire inspection is required.   

[Physical page 6](</Users/mcoors/Documents/Project Geode/MasterLegalDatabase/research/local_review/colorado-springs-construction-fees-qa-2026-09-12/images/page-6.png>)


**DEF-PERFORMANCE**

Performance Based Design Surcharge: A one-time fee to establish fire safety and engineering goals and <br>objectives, fire model construction and evaluation, plan review, inspection, acceptance testing, and re-<br>evaluation of all performance-based designs, alternative materials and methods or other design <br>alternatives when requested or at the plan reviewer’s discretion based on project scope.  In all cases the <br>minimum fee shall be $2,000.  

[Physical page 6](</Users/mcoors/Documents/Project Geode/MasterLegalDatabase/research/local_review/colorado-springs-construction-fees-qa-2026-09-12/images/page-6.png>)


**DEF-PRELIMINARY**

Preliminary Inspection: A preliminary inspection fee is assessed when a business or contractor requests an <br>inspector to perform a site evaluation of the scope of work to determine if work is being performed to all <br>applicable codes and standards.   

[Physical page 6](</Users/mcoors/Documents/Project Geode/MasterLegalDatabase/research/local_review/colorado-springs-construction-fees-qa-2026-09-12/images/page-6.png>)


**DEF-PREPLAN**

Pre-Plan Submittal Consult: Time associated with a project during the design and planning stages. The <br>assessed amount is cost recovery for staff during the consultation, similar to time spent during a plan <br>review. A fee will not be assessed for meetings requiring thirty minutes or less. 

[Physical page 6](</Users/mcoors/Documents/Project Geode/MasterLegalDatabase/research/local_review/colorado-springs-construction-fees-qa-2026-09-12/images/page-6.png>)


**DEF-REINSPECTION**

Re-Inspection: A fee assessed if an inspection is scheduled and any portion of the work is incomplete, <br>and/or hazards are not abated in an allotted timeframe. Failure to provide access for a requested <br>inspection, failure to maintain work in an exposed condition until the inspection is completed, deviation <br>from approved plans, lack of sufficient documentation or required equipment or personnel to conduct the 

[Physical page 6](</Users/mcoors/Documents/Project Geode/MasterLegalDatabase/research/local_review/colorado-springs-construction-fees-qa-2026-09-12/images/page-6.png>)

inspection, or a system that has not been pre-tested shall also require a re-inspection. 

[Physical page 7](</Users/mcoors/Documents/Project Geode/MasterLegalDatabase/research/local_review/colorado-springs-construction-fees-qa-2026-09-12/images/page-7.png>)

One definition continues from physical page 6 onto page 7. Both parts must travel together.

**DEF-TRIP**

Trip Fee: Accounts for time associated with two inspections for a given permit. Sprinkler contractors shall <br>be allowed three inspections per permit issued. A trip fee will be assessed when additional inspections are <br>required due to the phasing or scheduling of a project. 

[Physical page 7](</Users/mcoors/Documents/Project Geode/MasterLegalDatabase/research/local_review/colorado-springs-construction-fees-qa-2026-09-12/images/page-7.png>)


**DEF-WUI-COMMERCIAL**

Wildland Urban Interface (WUI) commercial surcharge: A WUI surcharge will be added to all applicable <br>commercial construction projects that are within CSFD’s WUI area.  This fee is in addition to the fee shown <br>in this fee schedule based on the occupancy class and square footage of the building.   

[Physical page 7](</Users/mcoors/Documents/Project Geode/MasterLegalDatabase/research/local_review/colorado-springs-construction-fees-qa-2026-09-12/images/page-7.png>)


